# Articles

Apply when editing **reader-facing articles** (essays under topic folders, `blog/*.md`). **Not** investigations, `page.md` indices, or dossiers unless asked.

**Full canon:** [`docs/instructions/ARTICLES.md`](../../docs/instructions/ARTICLES.md)

## Compact

- Links: Substack URL when the target essay has a `**Substack:**` post; otherwise **`https://paradigmthreat.net/...`**. Images always on **`https://paradigmthreat.net/...`**.
- Voice: **chronicle / documentary** — who did what, in order; **`I`** only for personal witness; no poetry, no manifesto cadence, no “this essay argues,” no **ordering the reader around** (**“Stop treating… Treat them as…,”** **“Read X as Y,”** **“Hunt the… Do not wait…”**). State the claim; the reader decides.
- Prefer Ari’s spoken wording from chat; do not upgrade it into verse. Same bar for comment replies: [plain-spoken prose](plain-spoken-prose.mdc).
- Proof density and **Limits** live in **`investigations/`** dossiers — articles summarize and link.
- Prefer cross-linking other **articles**; link dossiers only as companion receipts.
- **Claim fact-check on revise:** check each citation and each knock-downable argument (seat counts, thresholds, dates, ratios, who said it), not the essay as a mood. A live link used unclearly is the same fail: a stranger could hear agreement the pages do not share, a wider count than the page gives, or proof of the neighboring sentence. Author and model both get these wrong. Investigations may stay wrong and open. Articles ship polished. Body states the correct fact once; the check note goes in **`## LLM comments`** or the dossier. Canon: [`ARTICLES.md` → Claim fact-check](../../docs/instructions/ARTICLES.md#claim-fact-check-required-on-revise).
- **Sentence bridging:** the fix when a fact-check finds a cite used unclearly. Name said. Name said. is not a relation. If the next sentence is a different speaker or a different claim, the sentence says how it sits against the one before it. **However** when they diverge. **And** or **the same line** when they agree. No extra word when it is just the next fact. Do not add a caption that explains the bridge. A real **however** stays; the canned “not A, it is B” still goes. Canon: [`ARTICLES.md` → Voice → Sentence bridging](../../docs/instructions/ARTICLES.md#voice-who-we-are-writing-for).
- Run **`npm run autogen`** after substantive edits.
- Tone model when narrating: [`governance/war/the-great-depression-was-planned.md`](../../governance/war/the-great-depression-was-planned.md).
- **No correction archaeology in article bodies:** state the correct fact once; never ship “— not X”, “SRT-corrected”, or other agent-mistake scars. Hygiene belongs in the companion investigation. See [articles-no-correction-meta](articles-no-correction-meta.mdc) and ARTICLES.md drafting-process meta.
